  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Scope**\n\nI\'m focused on defining the project scope, understanding that RSU Siloam/Siloam Hospitals Ambon needs a company profile web application. I\'m carefully reviewing the provided materials to understand the intended purpose and essential features. Initial assessment suggests a straightforward presentation of information, but details still need to be fleshed out.\n\n\n**Clarifying Functionality**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the presentation teams\' needs, envisioning a web app mimicking PowerPoint slides for seamless navigation. The crucial addition is the dynamic doctor schedule integration, and I am parsing the user\'s requirements closely. I\'ve begun to analyze the provided slides, noting the splash screen and the \"CENTER OF EXCELLENCE\" slide, which has several options related to medical procedures.\n\n\n**Analyzing Data Requirements**\n\nI\'m now diving into specific data points and their presentation. I\'ve noted the birth statistics since December 2020 and the various medical procedures. The third slide\'s chart with 2023-2025 statistics for outpatient, inpatient, surgeries, emergency, and medical checkups is particularly insightful. I also have identified the chart format and data to be included. Furthermore, I\'ve identified the \"Our Facilities\" slides.\n\n\n**Detailing Hospital Features**\n\nI am now focusing on the hospital\'s facilities. I\'ve noted the room types (\"VVIP\", \"VIP\", \"Kelas I\", \"Kelas 2\", \"Kelas 3\") and the \"Executive Clinic\". I am specifically noting medical equipment like ESWL, PCNL & MIP, C-Arm, CT SCAN, Phaco, and the Surgery Microscope, all of which will be pivotal to address in the presentation. Finally, I\'ve outlined the future expansion plans for 2025 with the increased bed capacity and clinic additions.\n\n\n**Outlining Future Expansion**\n\nI\'ve just added the 2026-2028 expansion plans to my notes, including the addition of IPD floors and new services like Laparoscopy, Cath Lab, and MRI. I\'m now organizing the detailed \"Our Doctor\" section, categorizing physicians by specialty and meticulously recording their names and qualifications for accurate inclusion in the web application. This data will be critical for the \"Our Doctor\" section.\n\n\n**Cataloging Doctor Profiles**\n\nI\'m methodically entering doctor details from the provided slides. I have categorized them by specialization, double-checking for accuracy. I\'ve noted a slight inconsistency regarding the Endodontist specialization, so I\'m cross-referencing to resolve that.\n\n\n**Verifying Doctor Specializations**\n\nI\'m currently double-checking doctor specializations. I\'ve spotted a potential discrepancy in the provided materials regarding Ophthalmologists being incorrectly labeled as Endodontists. I\'ve categorized them accurately and ensured their correct specializations from the data. Specifically, I am ensuring to use accurate labels for them. I have organized them for inclusion in the \"Our Doctor\" section.\n\n\n**Compiling Doctor Information**\n\nI\'ve just added several more doctor profiles, focusing on orthopedic specialists, internists, and obstetricians. I\'ve also noted the anesthesiologists. The \"Our Social Media\" information is added. I am pleased to hear they will connect the doctor schedules dynamically, so I will now focus on anticipating how the data will be accessed.\n\n\n**Implementing Database Integration**\n\nNow, I\'m shifting focus to implementing a robust database system. Integrating a real database, like SQLite, JSON, or Firestore, presents a far superior solution. This will empower the hospital team to directly manage doctors, schedules, facilities, and charts, eliminating the need for manual code modifications. I\'m prioritizing an elegant slideshow view that mirrors the original slides\' aesthetic with responsive design.\n\n\n**Designing Presentation Flow**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in designing a dynamic, presentation-style interface. I envision arrow key navigation, click-based controls, or even swipes through beautiful, responsive slides. I\'m prioritizing a professional presentation navigation bar for seamless user experience. Furthermore, an \"Admin Panel\" will be incorporated for straightforward management of doctors, schedules, and hospital details.\n\n\n\n**Evaluating Database Strategy**\n\nI\'m now weighing the best database approach. My thoughts lean toward a local, editable JSON structure with an Express API, offering simplicity and ease of initial setup. This approach will satisfy the user\'s need for dynamic doctor schedule integration, ensuring future connectivity. The user\'s goal to connect to a separate database for doctor scheduling will be kept in mind, while I think about setting up the simple API. I\'m focusing on simplicity first, and will expand as needed.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Features**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the essential features for the web app. I\'m leaning toward a real web app presentation with an editable Admin Panel. This will enable persistent data storage on the server. I have the \"image-generation\" skill in mind to create high-quality placeholders for facilities and doctors if the slides lack real images. I\'m focusing on features such as a beautiful presentation with editable data fields.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 18
      nanos: 387521584
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
