  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Clarifying Application Architecture**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the project\'s architecture. The `package.json` reveals a client-side Vite setup, yet includes server-side dependencies like `express` and `tsx`. The instructions state a default to client-side if the user\'s architecture is unspecified. I\'m reconciling this apparent contradiction and determining the intended application structure.\n\n\n**Confirming Full-Stack Necessity**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to confirm the need for a full-stack approach. The database connection for automatic updates dictates this direction. An Express backend seems essential to persist changes to doctor schedules and expose an API. I\'m exploring API endpoints like `/api/doctors` for update flexibility. The directory structure lacks a `server.ts` file, so that\'s the next step.\n\n\n**Solidifying App Functionality**\n\nI\'ve got a robust plan! Adding scripts to `package.json` sets up development and build processes. I\'ll create `server.ts` to implement Vite middleware, handling development proxying and production static files. This enables a persistent JSON data store in `data/` via a new API router. This is going to be useful!\n\n\n**Defining Desired Presentation**\n\nI\'m now detailing the desired end product. My goal is to craft a polished slide presenter using Vite, React, Motion, and Tailwind, matching RSU Siloam\'s aesthetic with a clean light theme and deep blue/gold highlights. It\'ll provide a PowerPoint-like experience with slide navigation, full-screen, auto-play, and interactive dashboards, while dynamically displaying doctor schedules grouped by departments. I\'m focusing on the dynamic doctor schedule database, and how to represent it nicely.\n\n\n**Elaborating Feature Implementations**\n\nI\'m expanding on the interactive features. I\'m prioritizing real-time data updates, triggered by the \"Update Center,\" which will save to the backend API. I will include a doctor search, department filtering, and schedule viewing feature. I\'ll also add interactive facility slides, a dynamic Recharts visualization of patient trends, four-year roadmap timelines, and social media interactives, all driven by dynamic data. The database file to start is `metadata.json`.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 298699517
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
