  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating Project Build**\n\nI\'ve successfully installed `recharts`. Now, I\'m shifting focus to building the full-stack application as requested, aiming to connect with the user\'s doctor schedule database. The goal is to ensure the company profile updates automatically with doctor schedule updates, eliminating manual code adjustments. I\'m starting with server architecture.\n\n\n**Defining Data Structure**\n\nI\'ve formulated a simple, durable JSON-based REST API for data management. It\'s designed to run within the container, persisting data locally for speed and simplicity. The API includes endpoints for comprehensive data retrieval and updates, including specific doctor interactions (adding, modifying, deleting). I\'m confident this architecture will enable dynamic updates to the company profile. I\'m now crafting the default data state and mapping out categories for doctors and other slides (Centers of Excellence and Stats).\n\n\n**Cataloging Available Resources**\n\nI\'m now cataloging all the available medical resources and services. My current focus is on structuring and presenting the data on procedures (outpatient, inpatient, surgical, etc.) and facilities (Ambulance, Radiology, VVIP, etc.) effectively. I plan to organize them interactively, with photos and details. I\'ve also listed the doctors with their specialties.\n\n\n**Listing Doctor Specialties**\n\nI\'ve categorized the doctors by their specialties, creating organized lists for Obstetrics & Gynecology, Pediatrics, General Surgery, Urology, Cardiothoracic Surgery, Neurology, and Internal Medicine. This structuring is essential for the application to function effectively.\n\n\n**Expanding Doctor Categorization**\n\nI\'m now expanding the doctor categorization to include Dentistry, with specialties such as Prosthodontics, Oral Medicine, Pedodontics, Oral Surgery, and Endodontics. I\'m also adding Ophthalmologists, Cardiologists, Dermatologists and Physical Medicine Specialists, structuring them for efficient access within the application.\n\n\n**Adding Specialist Details**\n\nI\'ve just added several specialists to the doctor database, including Physical Medicine, Clinical Nutrition, Psychiatry, Surgical Oncology, and Anesthesiology. I\'ve designed the JSON schema with these as default data, ensuring the application launches with a robust foundation. I\'m now shifting focus to designing a flexible scheduling system, likely a weekly structure with specific time slots for each doctor.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 10
      nanos: 444400657
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
