  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Initial Data Structure**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the initial structure for the default database data file. I plan to store this data in a `/src/default_data.ts` representation. This way, if the data file is missing, I can copy it over during backend startup or write directly to it.\n\n\n**Refining Default Data Population**\n\nI\'ve decided to initialize the `/data/database.json` file directly with a default dataset. I\'m currently focused on populating this with realistic and editable doctor schedules. I\'m building a well-represented default doctor list, including OTOLARYNGOLOGISTS and PULMONOLOGISTS, complete with realistic schedules in a user-friendly format (e.g., \"Senin - Rabu 10:00 - 13:00\"). I am meticulously creating example doctor entries, and writing them directly.\n\n\n**Populating More Schedules**\n\nI\'m now expanding the default data with more detailed schedules. I\'m actively inputting doctors from various specializations into the example data. I have added schedules for Ina Angriany (Sp.P), Marisa Afifudin (Sp.P), Markus Daniel Taliak (Sp.OG), Rey Jauwerissa (Sp.OG), Irene Leha (Sp.OG), Ika Wiraswesty Ciptaningdiah (Sp.OG, M.Biomed), Norma Pattinama (Sp.OG), Rachmat Ramadhani Tuasikal (Sp.OG., SubSp.Onk), Erwin Rahakbauw (Sp.OG., SubSp.Onk) and am continuing on.\n\n\n**Adding More Doctors Now**\n\nI\'m now populating the default data with pediatricians and general surgeons. I am including schedules for dr. Robby Kalew, dr. Elizabeth Joan Salim, dr. Ria Resti Sukur, dr. Anitha Marllyin Mairuhu, and dr. Kartika Setiawaty. I am also working on adding schedules for general surgeons like dr. Mo Tualeka, dr. I Dewa Gede Sidan Agung Mahendra, dr. Ricky Masyudha, and dr. Hery Siswanto.\n\n\n**Expanding Schedule Inclusion**\n\nI am now focusing on expanding the default data with even more specialists. I\'ve just added schedules for urologists, cardiothoracic surgeons, neurologists, and internists. I am carefully documenting their schedules.\n\n\n**Adding More Doctors**\n\nI\'m now integrating more specialists into the default dataset. I have added schedules for internal medicine specialists, including dr. I Made Kristya Permana, dr. Alex Ranuseto, and dr. Ria Jauwerissa. I\'ve also just added the dentist and specialist schedules, and the data is looking well-represented now.\n\n\n**Finalizing Default Data Doctors**\n\nI\'m currently wrapping up the default dataset by adding schedules for more specialists. I\'ve now included schedules for clinical nutritionists, rehabilitation specialists, dermatologists, cardiologists, and ophthalmologists. The data file now looks complete and well-rounded.\n\n\n**Including More Doctors**\n\nI\'ve just added schedules for more specialists, now I\'m adding psychiatrists, surgical oncologists, and anaesthetists to complete the default data. The dataset is looking well-represented. I\'m excited with the completeness, and now plan to share the data file `/src/default_data_payload.ts` so both server-side and client-side can share the same information easily.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 53
      nanos: 879790443
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
