  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Facility Components**\n\nI\'ve moved on to examining the facility components presented on slides 4 through 8, focusing on screenshots related to the \"Our Facilities\" section. So far, the focus is on a 24-hour emergency service, and home care services. The facility descriptions include radiology and outpatient services, followed by inpatient services.\n\n\n**Developing UI Structure**\n\nI\'m now focused on translating the \"Our Facilities\" section into a React web app component, `/src/components/SlideFacilities.tsx`. The goal is to replicate the PowerPoint presentation\'s sub-slides precisely. I\'m thinking of incorporating a \"Sub-Slide Index\" (0-4) to mirror the structure of the original PPT slides. This ensures that the user can navigate through the information in the same way they would the original presentation.\n\n\n**Refining Slide Navigation**\n\nI\'ve decided to restructure the slide flow. Instead of sub-slides, \"Our Facilities\" will now occupy main slide slots 3 through 7. This decision aligns the UI with the PowerPoint\'s natural progression. I\'m aiming for a more intuitive user experience. Now, I\'m working to create a single, modular `/src/components/SlideFacilities.tsx` component that renders content based on a \"page\" prop, reducing code duplication.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 16
      nanos: 676833206
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
