  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Rendering Options**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how to render the \"Our Doctor\" slides from SlideDoctors. There are 30 distinct slides, and I\'m currently pondering various options for their representation, and how to best deliver them. I\'m prioritizing user experience and efficient display.\n\n\n**Analyzing Slide Structure**\n\nI\'ve been analyzing the \"Our Doctor\" slide structure. It\'s a series of doctor profile lists, each with a consistent layout: a vertical banner on the left with the specialty and elegant text, and doctor portraits with names and titles on the right. I\'m focusing on creating an interactive component in `/src/components/SlideDoctors.tsx` that uses a `specialtyGroupIndex` (0 to 22) or allows seamless flipping.\n\n\n**Mapping Specialty Indices**\n\nI\'ve just finished mapping specialty indices to the \"Our Doctor\" slides! The provided data maps perfectly. Now that I have the comprehensive index, I can finalize the data structure for the interactive component in `/src/components/SlideDoctors.tsx`. This includes the mapping of specialty to slide number, ensuring efficient retrieval and display.\n\n\n**Implementing Dynamic Display**\n\nI\'m now implementing dynamic display for the doctor slides! I realized I can use a single `slideOffset` prop in `/src/components/SlideDoctors.tsx` to handle all 31 slides. This approach allows me to instantly reflect database updates. I\'ve begun designing the 31 specialty groups by slicing the doctors into their correct groups! For example, Group 0 (Page 14) is for OTOLARYNGOLOGISTS (dr. Rodrigo, dr. Stanley, dr. Chriscelia), and I am currently mapping all 31, from 13 to 43.\n\n\n**Defining Specialty Groups**\n\nI\'m now defining the remaining specialty groups for the dynamic slide display. I\'ve successfully implemented Group 5 through Group 20, mapping doctors to their correct specialty pages, ensuring that the `/src/components/SlideDoctors.tsx` component will display the doctor groups accurately!\n\n\n**Refining Data Mapping**\n\nI\'m now refining the data mapping to ensure dynamic display accuracy. I\'ve finished the remaining specialty groups (21-30) and am considering a dynamic approach for doctor assignments. Instead of hardcoding, I am going to dynamically slice doctors from our master list based on their specialty, ensuring that updates from administrators are seamlessly reflected. I\'m focusing on their \'specialty\' or custom criteria for identification.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 26
      nanos: 823832885
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
